id: basic-attack
name: Basic Attack
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
profile: any
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Attack with any Profile. Strike against the target's Dodge; on a win, Wound
  less their Soak Value.

text: >
  Basic Attack Maneuver: Make a basic, unnamed attack.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: Varies (uses the Ki Point Cost of the chosen Profile)
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent with an Attacking Maneuver using a Profile (see —
  Foundations & Profiles) of your choice. If the Profile has an Area of Effect, use
  that to select the target(s) instead. You can only use each Profile once per Combat
  Round when using a Basic Attack Maneuver, except for the Simple Profile.

# One rule in the entry above is not enforced.
#
# "You can only use each Profile once per Combat Round when using a Basic Attack
# Maneuver, except for the Simple Profile." Nothing counts which Profiles have been
# used through a Basic Attack this round, so the picker offers all of them every
# time.
#
# Everything needed is here - a use is already recorded against the round it was
# spent in, which is what makes 1/Round work for a Maneuver - but this counts
# Profiles rather than Maneuvers, and nothing keeps that tally. Until it does, the
# table keeps it: the entry on the row says the rule, which is the part a player
# reads.

---
